<title>SWITZERLAND: Adecco unit grows in U.S. with Seagate buy.</title>
<headline>Adecco unit grows in U.S. with Seagate buy.</headline>
<dateline>LAUSANNE, Switzerland 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss-French part-time employment conglomerate Adecco SA said its subsidiary Lee Hecht Harrison had acquired Seagate Associates, Inc, giving it a total of over 16 outlets in the New York area.</p>
<p>Lee Hecht Harrison gained six Seagate offices in New Jersey and two in New York through the acquisition.</p>
<p>Worldwide, Lee Hecht Harrison now has 68 offices. Seagate, specialised in outplacement services, is based in New Jersey, and had a turnover in 1996 of $12 million.</p>
<p>Details of the transaction were not disclosed.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
